@startuml
title Inside SharedServices: the Gate facade, the navigator (via its proxy), and dispatch by subscription

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

package "SharedServices process" #fdfdfd {

  [Gate\na facade — the one client entrance] as GATE

  [UniversalNavigatorProxy\nthe navigator's stand-in;\nthe Gate holds this, not the navigator] as PROXY

  package "UniversalNavigator" #fbfdfd {
    [Triage + route\nreads the map;\nvalidates the selection;\ndrives the dispatch] as ROUTE
    [Render ledger\ndispatch owes a page;\ntimeout races the callback] as LEDGER
    [Merge — serial, deterministic\n(the library's function)] as MERGE
    [Session and\nsecurity helpers] as SEC
  }

  [UtteranceManager\nclassify: preamble + fragments ->\nthe set of tools to dispatch to;\ndecides sufficiency and dispatches if so\n----\nRequestUsersRefinement(): the UM's own LLM authors\nthe question — no dispatchable route or a missing slot\nRequestUsersRefinement(question): a dispatched tool\nauthored the question; the UM delivers it\n(one conversational surface — no tool talks to the user)] as UM

  package "Tools · ChatHealthyTool subclasses" #fbfdfd {
    [ProviderSearch] as T1
    [ProviderDetail] as T2
    [SpecialtyFilter] as T3
    [Geo\nresolves free-text geography] as T5
    [Selection · Facility\nTrials · ...] as T4
    [LockoutTool\nNOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE] as TL
  }
}

database "ToolRegistry\none record per build per env:\ntools, subscriptions, may_call,\nfragments, routes and proofs;\npages carry members / required_members / completeness" as REG #eef6f5
package "MongoDB (Atlas) · front-end cluster" #eef6f5 {
  database "Sessions and ledger" as SESS
  database "Registered Users" as USERS
}

GATE -down-> PROXY : token, head,\nparameters
PROXY -down-> ROUTE : forwards to\nthe navigator
ROUTE -[#9ca3af]up-> PROXY : merged document
PROXY -[#9ca3af]up-> GATE : stream the\nanswer back
ROUTE -right-> UM : classify:\nwhat to dispatch to

REG <-- ROUTE : reads the live\nmap at startup
REG <-[#9ca3af]- UM : fragments assembled\ninto the preamble

ROUTE -down-> LEDGER : dispatch\nby subscription
LEDGER -right-> MERGE
MERGE -up-> ROUTE : merged document
SEC -down-> SESS : validate once;\nstate as rows
SESS -[hidden]right- USERS

LEDGER -down-> T1
T1 -[#9ca3af]up-> LEDGER : completion callback\ncloses the entry

T1 -[hidden]right- T2
T2 -[hidden]right- T3
T3 -[hidden]right- T5
T5 -[hidden]right- T4
T4 -[hidden]right- TL

note left of GATE
  Knows transport exists; nothing else does.
  Collects the request's facts and passes them
  on; streams what comes back. Verifies nothing
  itself — the navigator's helpers own security.
  Five call types cross this entrance, each with
  a required proof: our_signature / api_key +
  credential / session_token / none.
end note

note bottom of PROXY
  The Gate reaches the navigator only through
  this proxy; the proxy is the navigator's face,
  in-process or across the boundary alike.
end note

note bottom of TL
  A tool declares exactly one of a routing fragment
  or NOT_UTTERANCE_ROUTABLE. Silence refuses the
  build, so a safety tool's unreachability is a
  decision, never an omission.

  Lockout is DETERMINISTIC, not probabilistic: the
  classifier runs at temperature 0, and an exact
  repeat of a recorded lockout utterance
  (Users.UserLockOutUtterances — UPPERCASED + count)
  is a deterministic lockout, then human-curated by
  ChatHealthy staff (monthly frequency-ordered
  report). Full mechanism: C2 Security.
end note

note right of MERGE
  A conflict between two returning
  documents is an exception,
  never last-writer-wins.
end note
@enduml
